====================================================================================================
CBO-GAP onsetclass -- what kind of bend each H3 onset is (N43), read-only
====================================================================================================
  onsetclass sha256 81ce406d397d6286d499ecd42a0d79f1dcf0b683cf63b0d86113849c760eb541
  onsetdiag sha256  ad337adc7a8ecb70109b24bdabc4942f8613e45e90592f6921977863b22b4041
  rerunlib sha256   6a7ddf42242d5101086741e3a341db9711b2d47fdbfd60710be9229de8895b07
  python 3.12.3   numpy 2.5.3   platform Linux-7.0.0-38-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.39   workers 2
  --n39 runs/rerun-analysis-20261025-051314   --twenty runs/rerun-analysis-20261027-185918   archive /home/rahul/Research/cbo-gap-final/zenodo-v1
  writes nothing; no seed (nothing random); point S-slopes only, no bootstrap

  What this prints, in plain words. Each H3 onset is where one bend fits a curve of
  S-slope against log r best. A bend can sit where a rise starts, where it ends, or
  where a rise already under way gets steeper, and the onset number alone does not
  say which. For every onset of ONSET (probe beta) and ONSET-CAL (fixed beta), 80 in
  all, and for round 1's ten, this script measures the net rise of the curve up to
  the bend ('before') and from the bend to r = 3.0 ('after'), and names the bend by
  comparing both with the margin m. A rise is the slope moving from -1 toward 0.

  THE RULE IS POST HOC. It was fixed by Claude on 2026-10-28 (ledger N43) after the
  curves of the 25 onsets at 2.00, the isotropic d 80 mean curves and round 1's ten
  mean curves had been seen. Its extension to bends below 2.0 was written on 2026-10-28
  before any of the other 55 was computed. It describes the point curves; it is not
  a test. Rule: before = y(onset) - y(0.75); after = y(3.0) - y(onset);
    start      after > m, before <= m      end      before > m, after <= m
    continues  both > m                    no rise  both <= m
    line       onset 0.75: a bend at the first point is a straight line, no bend
  dist = the smaller of |before - m| and |after - m|: the call cannot change unless m
  moves by at least dist.

